n Jerauld County runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids January to February came in under 90% of normal in 39 of 75 years. In 2025 that same pair hit 20% of normal on the middle, and so far in 2026 it sits at 16%. Every grid had its driest year in 1976, with grid 28925 down at 48% of normal.</p>"}
